<h2 id="deal">The Extension</h2>
<p>Williams and the Cowboys agreed Monday, August 10 on a three-year extension worth $105.9 million, including $101 million guaranteed — $63.35 million of it guaranteed at signing, plus a $31.85 million signing bonus. The deal locks him in through the 2030 season and makes him the second-highest-paid defensive tackle in the league, trailing only Philadelphia's Jalen Carter. Williams joined Dallas at last season's trade deadline in a deal that sent a 2027 first-round pick, a 2026 second-round pick, and defensive tackle Mazi Smith back to the Jets, who drafted him third overall in 2019.</p>
