<h2 id="combine">The Combine Profile</h2>
<p>Williams entered the 2019 draft at 6-foot-3 and 303 pounds, and ran a 4.83-second 40-yard dash — the fastest time among all interior defensive linemen at that combine, a full tenth of a second ahead of the next-closest player at his position. He backed that up with a 30.5-inch vertical jump and a broad jump of 9 feet, 4 inches, both well above what's typical for a defensive tackle north of 300 pounds. A finger injury kept him out of bench press testing, but nothing else in his profile suggested any limitation.</p>
